    "causal_explanation": "The native-width ANYEXT legality table omitted s8/s16/s32-to-s64 cases. Route them through existing ZEXT lowering, choosing zero for unspecified high bits. The original preprocessed input and identical retained LLVM IR pass after this backend rule change; the reduced masked-byte store independently fails the captured baseline at G_ANYEXT and passes the candidate. Default-mode rules are unchanged.",
    "trigger_check": "Retained prelegalizer MIR captures the backend input; the seven-line valid masked-byte IR reaches s8-to-s64 ANYEXT during legalization. The recovered C stages pass 36 verifier compilations across six optimization levels and three width modes. Host and bsnes-jg default/a16/xy16 agree for all-count shifts (0x6A2B) and the recovered variable-shift bitboard probe (0x479E). Identical retained LTO bitcode fails with the preserved pre-0055 LLD at G_ANYEXT, links with rebuilt LLD, and executes at 0x479E in all three modes. Installed LLD matches the rebuilt hash.",
